---
import Arrow from "~/components/Arrow.astro";
import Button from "~/components/Button.astro";
import CommonContent from "~/components/CommonContent.astro";
import {
	cfpCloseDate,
	cfpOpenDate,
	cfpResponseDate,
	eventDate,
} from "~/data/event";
import { links } from "~/data/links";
import { currentYear } from "~/data/years";
import ArticleLayout from "~/layouts/ArticleLayout.astro";

const opens = `${cfpOpenDate}, ${currentYear - 1}`;
const closes = `${cfpCloseDate}, ${currentYear}`;
const responds = `${cfpResponseDate}, ${currentYear}`;

const topicAreas = [
	[`Accessibility`, `the accessibility tree, WCAG, web accessibility`],
	[`AI`, `agentic software, tools made for AI agents`],
	[`Building`, `CLI tools, deployments, monorepo management`],
	[
		`Documentation`,
		`writing docs, tools to manage and/or share them, explaining code`,
	],
	[
		`Editors`,
		`tools such as IDEs along with integrations and plugins built on them`,
	],
	[
		`Open Source`,
		`the making, maintenance, release, and socialization of shared software`,
	],
	[`Performance`, `enhancing performance of apps, sites, or any web dev tools`],
	[`Runtimes`, `execution environments such as Bun, Deno, and Node.js`],
	[
		`Testing`,
		`the art of verifying code, or building tools to help developers test`,
	],
	[`Tooling`, `debuggers, integrations, and general dev tools themselves`],
	[
		`Other`,
		`something fun or incredible - we love off-the-beaten-trail fun things`,
	],
];

const languageAreas = [
	[`Rust`, `working in Rust for the purposes of web dev apps and/or tooling`],
	[
		`TypeScript`,
		`integrating, working with, or even contributing to our favorite JS superset`,
	],
	[`WebAssembly`, `tooling or usage of WebAssembly/WASI/WASM`],
	[`Native Languages`, `we've accepted talks on Go, Zig, C++, and more`],
	[`New Languages`, `SquiggleConf is a home for new tech - show us!`],
];
---

<ArticleLayout
	article={{
		description:
			"Advice and general information for submitting talks to SquiggleConf",
		title: "Call for Proposals",
	}}
	squiggly="wide"
>
	<Fragment slot="lead">
		Thank you so much for your interest in speaking at SquiggleConf{" "}
		{currentYear}! This page is a general guide for what you can expect in
		submitting, including tips for what we're looking for.
	</Fragment>

	<Fragment slot="intro">
		<div class="apply-actions">
			<Button
				as="a"
				class="apply-button"
				href={links.cfp}
				size="large"
				target="_blank"
				variant="emphasized"
			>
				Apply to the CFP here!
				<Arrow />
			</Button>
		</div>
	</Fragment>

	<CommonContent heading="CFP Highlights">
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>📆 Deadline:</strong> Submit your proposal by {closes}. You'll
				hear from us by {responds}.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>🤝 Acceptance:</strong> If we accept your talk, we'll ask you to
				confirm within 7 days of hearing from us.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>🧠 Experience:</strong> Speakers of all experience levels,
				including first-timers, are encouraged to apply. We prioritize substance
				above all else.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>👍 Expectations:</strong> Leading up to the conference, helping
				us promote your talk. Giving us a remote dry run of a rough draft of
				your talk two weeks before the conference.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<h3>Conference Details</h3>

		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>🗺️ Time & Place:</strong>
				{eventDate}
				{currentYear} in Boston, Massachusetts. The Simons Theater at the New
				England Aquarium, right on the ocean coastline in the very center of
				downtown Boston.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>🗣️ Format:</strong> In-person, either a 30 minute talk + 5
				minutes for audience questions, or a 10 minute lightning talk.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>✈️ Covered:</strong> We can cover travel and accommodations for
				speakers, though we have a limited budget and prefer companies to pay if
				possible. We can work with you.
			</li>
		</ul>
	</CommonContent>

	<CommonContent heading="CFP Timeline">
		<p>We will respond to every talk proposal submitted.</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>{opens}:</strong> CFP opens
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>{closes}:</strong> CFP closes
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>{responds}:</strong> All CFP submitters will have heard back
				from us
			</li>
		</ul>
		<p>
			If we accept your submission, we will expect you to accept or reject our
			invitation within a week of hearing from us.
		</p>
		<p>
			We will create a "marketing title" for your talk with you that will be
			used to advertise your talk. There may be a completely different title
			used for the YouTube video.
		</p>
	</CommonContent>

	<CommonContent heading="Speaker Expectations">
		<p>
			The <a href="/articles/speaker-guide">speaker guide</a> covers what to
			expect as a SquiggleConf speaker, including the information we'll need
			from you, your schedule around the conference, and travel and
			accommodations.
		</p>
		<p>
			<strong>
				We require a remote dry run of your presentation two weeks before the
				conference.
			</strong>{" "}
			This will help us check talks for accessibility best practices.
		</p>
	</CommonContent>

	<CommonContent heading="Tips and Tricks">
		<p>
			We suggest reading{" "}
			<a
				href="https://www.joshuakgoldberg.com/blog/how-i-apply-to-conferences/?utm-source=squiggleconfcfp"
				target="_blank"
			>
				this CFP help guide
			</a>{" "}
			for an overview of how to submit to a CFP.
		</p>

		<h3>Asking for Help</h3>

		<p>
			We're always happy to give advice and generally help in submitting to the
			CFP! There are no "dumb" questions.
		</p>
		<p>
			Please don't hesitate to reach out to{" "}
			<a href={links.cfpQuestionsEmail}>cfp@squiggleconf.com</a> or in the
			#cfp-questions channel of the{" "}
			<a href={links.discord}>SquiggleConf Discord</a>. That includes asking us
			about a few ideas before spending the time to write up a full proposal.
		</p>

		<h3>Multiple Proposals</h3>

		<p>
			Feel free to submit multiple proposals, but please limit it to your top
			three.
		</p>

		<h3>Timing</h3>

		<p>
			We don't factor in how early or late a CFP is submitted. We recommend not
			procrastinating until the last minute, so you don't forget to submit.
		</p>

		<h3>Topic Suggestions</h3>

		<p>
			Most of all, we're looking for interesting talks on interesting topics in
			the developer tooling space. Our suggested categories with example focuses
			are:
		</p>
		<ul>
			{topicAreas.map(([topic, description]) => (
				<li>
					<strong>{topic}:</strong> {description}
				</li>
			))}
		</ul>
		<p>We're also interested in talks on languages:</p>
		<ul>
			{languageAreas.map(([topic, description]) => (
				<li>
					<strong>{topic}:</strong> {description}
				</li>
			))}
		</ul>
		<p>We are not looking for talks whose primary focus is:</p>
		<ul>
			<li>
				<strong>Shilling:</strong> Shilling can be good, but it usually isn't.
				See how we think about it in the{" "}
				<a href="/articles/speaker-guide#shilling">speaker guide</a>.
			</li>
			<li>
				<strong>Blockchain/Crypto/NFTs:</strong> We doubt these will be
				applicable and useful, but we are open minded and welcome you to make
				your case.
			</li>
		</ul>

		<div class="apply-actions">
			<Button
				as="a"
				class="apply-button"
				href={links.cfp}
				size="large"
				target="_blank"
				variant="emphasized"
			>
				Apply to the CFP here!
				<Arrow />
			</Button>
		</div>
	</CommonContent>
</ArticleLayout>

<style>
	.apply-actions {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: center;
		margin: 2rem 0 1rem;
	}

	.apply-button {
		gap: 0.5rem;
	}
</style>
